  <div slot="started">
    <p>
      Dry Duck’s owner is John, the same operator behind Rewired, which lowered partnership risk.
      He’d already proven he can build toward multi-million run rates. What we hadn’t done together
      was launch a category-new company from pure ideation with an AI-accelerated website and SEO
      system.
    </p>
    <p>
      The experiment fee was intentionally small (on the order of a few hundred dollars for the
      initial build). The bet wasn’t “AI magic.” It was: encode everything we already know about
      local Google into a shippable system, fast.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The month-two cliff (and why it matters)</h2>
  <p>
    New Google profiles and domains often get an early visibility surge, then a brutal average-out.
    Dry Duck crushed early, staffed and equipped into that momentum, then watched leads fall off a
    cliff in month two. Month three organic returned, weaker than the launch spike but real, and
    the climb resumed as rankings matured and ads entered the mix.
  </p>
  <p>
    That pattern is why we don’t treat a hot first month as permanent capacity.
    and why foundation quality still matters when the honeymoon ends.
  </p>
